#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Isang libreng kursong IBM tungkol sa quantum information at computation"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inner products and projections"
msgstr "Mga inner product at projection"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr, operatorname */}\n"
"To better prepare ourselves to explore the capabilities and limitations of quantum circuits, we now introduce some additional mathematical concepts — namely the *inner product* between vectors (and its connection to the Euclidean norm), the notions of *orthogonality* and *orthonormality* for sets of vectors, and *projection* matrices, which will allow us to introduce a handy generalization of standard basis measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr, operatorname */}\n"
"Para mas maging handa sa pag-explore ng mga kakayahan at limitasyon ng quantum circuits, ipinapakilala natin ngayon ang ilang karagdagang konsepto sa matematika — ang *inner product* sa pagitan ng mga vector (at ang koneksyon nito sa Euclidean norm), ang mga konsepto ng *orthogonality* at *orthonormality* para sa mga set ng vector, at ang mga *projection* matrix, na magbibigay-daan sa atin na ipakilala ang isang kapaki-pakinabang na generalisasyon ng standard basis measurements.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inner products {#inner-products}"
msgstr "Mga inner product {#inner-products}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recall that when we use the Dirac notation to refer to an arbitrary column vector as a ket, such as\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na kapag ginagamit natin ang Dirac notation para tukuyin ang isang arbitrary na column vector bilang ket, tulad ng\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "the corresponding bra vector is the *conjugate transpose* of this vector:\n"
msgstr "ang katumbas na bra vector ay ang *conjugate transpose* ng vector na ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternatively, if we have some classical state set $\\Sigma$ in mind, and we express a column vector as a ket,\n"
"such as\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilang alternatibo, kung mayroon tayong classical state set na $\\Sigma$ sa isip, at isinasalita natin ang isang column vector bilang ket,\n"
"tulad ng\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then the corresponding row (or bra) vector is the conjugate transpose\n"
msgstr "ang katumbas na row vector (o bra vector) ay ang conjugate transpose\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also have that the product of a bra vector and a ket vector, viewed as matrices either having a single row or a single column, results in a scalar.\n"
"Specifically, if we have two column vectors\n"
msgstr ""
"Mayroon din tayong resulta na ang product ng isang bra vector at isang ket vector, na tinitingnan bilang mga matrix na may iisang row o iisang column, ay nagreresulta sa isang scalar.\n"
"Partikular, kung mayroon tayong dalawang column vector\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so that the row vector $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ is as in equation $(1)$, then\n"
msgstr "kung kaya ang row vector na $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ ay gaya ng nasa equation $(1)$, ay\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\beta_1 + \\cdots + \\overline{\\alpha_n}\\beta_n.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\beta_1 + \\cdots + \\overline{\\alpha_n}\\beta_n.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, if we have two column vectors that we have written as\n"
msgstr "Bilang alternatibo, kung mayroon tayong dalawang column vector na nasulat bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so that $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ is the row vector $(2)$, we find that\n"
msgstr "kung kaya ang $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ ay ang row vector $(2)$, mahahanap natin na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b\\rangle\\Biggr)\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_b \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b\\rangle\\Biggr)\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_b \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the last equality follows from the observation that $\\langle a \\vert a \\rangle = 1$ and $\\langle a \\vert b \\rangle = 0$ for classical states $a$ and $b$ satisfying $a\\neq b$.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang huling pagkakapantay-pantay ay sumusunod mula sa obserbasyon na $\\langle a \\vert a \\rangle = 1$ at $\\langle a \\vert b \\rangle = 0$ para sa mga classical state na $a$ at $b$ na tumutugon sa $a\\neq b$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The value $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle$ is called the *inner product* between the vectors $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Inner products are critically important in quantum information and computation;\n"
"we would not get far in understanding quantum information at a mathematical level without them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang value na $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle$ ay tinatawag na *inner product* sa pagitan ng mga vector na $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ at $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Ang mga inner product ay kritikal na mahalaga sa quantum information at computation;\n"
"hindi tayo malayo sa pag-unawa ng quantum information sa antas ng matematika nang wala ang mga ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us now collect together some basic facts about inner products of vectors.\n"
msgstr "Narito ang ilang pangunahing katotohanan tungkol sa mga inner product ng vector.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Relationship to the Euclidean norm.** The inner product of any vector\n"
msgstr "**Kaugnayan sa Euclidean norm.** Ang inner product ng anumang vector\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   with itself is\n"
msgstr "   sa kanyang sarili ay\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\alpha_a\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert\\alpha_a\\vert^2\n"
"   = \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\alpha_a\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert\\alpha_a\\vert^2\n"
"   = \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Thus, the Euclidean norm of a vector may alternatively be expressed as\n"
msgstr "   Kaya, ang Euclidean norm ng isang vector ay maaari ring isalita bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| = \\sqrt{ \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle }.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| = \\sqrt{ \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle }.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Notice that the Euclidean norm of a vector must always be a nonnegative real number.\n"
"   Moreover, the only way the Euclidean norm of a vector can be equal to zero is if every one of the entries is equal to zero, which is to say that the vector is the zero vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Pansinin na ang Euclidean norm ng isang vector ay laging isang non-negatibong tunay na numero.\n"
"   Bukod dito, ang tanging paraan para ang Euclidean norm ng isang vector ay maging zero ay kung ang bawat isa sa mga entry nito ay zero, ibig sabihin, ang vector ay ang zero vector.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   We can summarize these observations like this: for every vector $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ we have\n"
msgstr "   Maaari nating ibuod ang mga obserbasyon na ito tulad nito: para sa bawat vector na $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ ay mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   with $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$ if and only if $\\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$.\n"
"   This property of the inner product is sometimes referred to as _positive definiteness_.\n"
msgstr ""
"   kung saan ang $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$ kung at tanging kung ang $\\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$.\n"
"   Ang property na ito ng inner product ay minsan tinatawag na _positive definiteness_.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Conjugate symmetry.** For any two vectors\n"
msgstr "**Conjugate symmetry.** Para sa anumang dalawang vector\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   we have\n"
msgstr "   mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\beta_a} \\alpha_a,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\beta_a} \\alpha_a,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   and therefore\n"
msgstr "   at samakatuwid\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\overline{\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle} = \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\overline{\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle} = \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Linearity in the second argument (and conjugate linearity in the first).**\n"
"Let us suppose that $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$, $\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle$, and $\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle$ are vectors and $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_2$ are complex numbers. If we define a new vector\n"
msgstr ""
"**Linearity sa ikalawang argument (at conjugate linearity sa una).**\n"
"Ipagpalagay na ang $\\vert \\psi \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle,$ at $\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle$ ay mga vector at ang $\\alpha_1$ at $\\alpha_2$ ay mga complex number. Kung tatukuyin natin ang bagong vector\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\phi\\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\phi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\phi_2\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\phi\\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\phi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\phi_2\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   then\n"
msgstr "   ay\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigl( \\alpha_1\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"   = \\alpha_1 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigl( \\alpha_1\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"   = \\alpha_1 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   That is to say, the inner product is _linear_ in the second argument.\n"
"   This can be verified either through the formulas above or simply by noting that matrix multiplication is linear in each argument (and specifically in the second argument).\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ibig sabihin, ang inner product ay _linear_ sa ikalawang argument.\n"
"   Maaari itong mapatunayan sa pamamagitan ng mga formula sa itaas o simpleng pagtukoy na ang matrix multiplication ay linear sa bawat argument (at partikular sa ikalawang argument).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Combining this fact with conjugate symmetry reveals that the inner product is _conjugate linear_ in the first argument. That is, if $\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle$, $\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle$, and $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ are vectors and $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_2$ are complex numbers, and we define\n"
msgstr "   Ang pagsasama ng katotohanang ito kasama ang conjugate symmetry ay nagpapakita na ang inner product ay _conjugate linear_ sa unang argument. Ibig sabihin, kung ang $\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,$ at $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ ay mga vector at ang $\\alpha_1$ at $\\alpha_2$ ay mga complex number, at tinutukuyin natin ang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\bigl( \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\bigr)\n"
"   \\vert\\phi\\rangle\n"
"   = \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert \\phi \\rangle + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\phi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\bigl( \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\bigr)\n"
"   \\vert\\phi\\rangle\n"
"   = \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert \\phi \\rangle + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\phi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The Cauchy–Schwarz inequality.**\n"
"For every choice of vectors $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ having the same number of entries, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang Cauchy–Schwarz inequality.**\n"
"Para sa bawat pagpipilian ng mga vector na $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ at $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ na may parehong bilang ng mga entry, mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\vert \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\bigr| \\leq \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| \\bigl\\| \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   \\bigr\\|.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\vert \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\bigr| \\leq \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| \\bigl\\| \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   \\bigr\\|.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   This is an incredibly handy inequality that gets used quite extensively in quantum information (and in many other topics of study).\n"
msgstr "   Ito ay isang napaka-kapaki-pakinabang na inequality na malawakang ginagamit sa quantum information (at sa marami pang ibang paksa ng pag-aaral).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Orthogonal and orthonormal sets {#orthogonal-and-orthonormal-sets}"
msgstr "Mga orthogonal at orthonormal na set {#orthogonal-and-orthonormal-sets}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two vectors $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ are said to be *orthogonal* if their inner product is zero:\n"
msgstr "Ang dalawang vector na $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ at $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ ay tinatawag na *orthogonal* kung ang kanilang inner product ay zero:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Geometrically, we can think about orthogonal vectors as vectors at right angles to each other.\n"
msgstr "Sa geometrika na paraan, maaari nating isipin ang mga orthogonal na vector bilang mga vector na nasa tamang anggulo sa isa't isa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A set of vectors $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is called an *orthogonal set* if every vector in the set is orthogonal to every other vector in the set.\n"
"That is, this set is orthogonal if\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang set ng mga vector na $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ ay tinatawag na *orthogonal set* kung ang bawat vector sa set ay orthogonal sa bawat ibang vector sa set.\n"
"Ibig sabihin, orthogonal ang set na ito kung\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle = 0\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle = 0\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for all choices of $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ for which $j\\neq k$.\n"
msgstr "para sa lahat ng pagpipilian ng $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ kung saan ang $j\\neq k$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A set of vectors $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is called an *orthonormal* set if it is an orthogonal set and, in addition, every vector in the set is a unit vector.\n"
"Alternatively, this set is an orthonormal set if we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang set ng mga vector na $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ ay tinatawag na *orthonormal* set kung ito ay isang orthogonal set at, bukod dito, ang bawat vector sa set ay isang unit vector.\n"
"Bilang alternatibo, ang set na ito ay isang orthonormal set kung mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & j = k\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & j\\neq k\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & j = k\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & j\\neq k\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for all choices of $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$.\n"
msgstr "para sa lahat ng pagpipilian ng $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, a set $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is an *orthonormal basis* if, in addition to being an orthonormal set, it forms a basis.\n"
"This is equivalent to $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ being an orthonormal set and $m$ being equal to the dimension of the space from which $\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ are drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, ang isang set na $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ ay isang *orthonormal basis* kung, bukod sa pagiging orthonormal set, ito ay nagbubuo ng isang basis.\n"
"Katumbas ito ng $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ na isang orthonormal set at ang $m$ ay katumbas ng dimensyon ng espasyo kung saan kinuha ang $\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, for any classical state set $\\Sigma$, the set of all standard basis vectors\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa, para sa anumang classical state set na $\\Sigma$, ang set ng lahat ng standard basis vector\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\big\\{ \\vert a \\rangle \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\big\\{ \\vert a \\rangle \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is an orthonormal basis.\n"
"The set $\\{\\vert+\\rangle,\\vert-\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis for the $2$-dimensional space corresponding to a single qubit, and the Bell basis $\\{\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\phi^-\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis for the $4$-dimensional space corresponding to two qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"ay isang orthonormal basis.\n"
"Ang set na $\\{\\vert+\\rangle,\\vert-\\rangle\\}$ ay isang orthonormal basis para sa $2$-dimensional na espasyo na katumbas ng iisang qubit, at ang Bell basis na $\\{\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\phi^-\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\}$ ay isang orthonormal basis para sa $4$-dimensional na espasyo na katumbas ng dalawang qubit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extending orthonormal sets to orthonormal bases {#extending-orthonormal-sets-to-orthonormal-bases}"
msgstr "Pagpapalawak ng mga orthonormal set sa mga orthonormal basis {#extending-orthonormal-sets-to-orthonormal-bases}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ are vectors that live in an $n$-dimensional space, and assume moreover that $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal set.\n"
"Orthonormal sets are always linearly independent sets, so these vectors necessarily span a subspace of dimension $m$.\n"
"From this we conclude that $m\\leq n$ because the dimension of the subspace spanned by these vectors cannot be larger than the dimension of the entire space from which they're drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipagpalagay na ang $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ ay mga vector na nabubuhay sa isang $n$-dimensional na espasyo, at ipagpalagay pa na ang $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ ay isang orthonormal set.\n"
"Ang mga orthonormal set ay laging linearly independent set, kaya ang mga vector na ito ay kinakailangang sumasaklaw sa isang subspace na may dimensyong $m$.\n"
"Mula dito ay maaari nating masimpulan na ang $m\\leq n$ dahil ang dimensyon ng subspace na sinasaklaw ng mga vector na ito ay hindi maaaring mas malaki kaysa sa dimensyon ng buong espasyong pinagkukunan nito.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If it is the case that $m<n$, then it is always possible to choose an additional $n-m$ vectors\n"
"$\\vert \\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ so that\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ forms an orthonormal basis.\n"
"A procedure known as the *Gram–Schmidt orthogonalization process* can be used to construct these vectors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung sakaling ang $m<n$, palagi itong posible na pumili ng karagdagang $n-m$ na vector\n"
"na $\\vert \\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ upang\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ ay bumuo ng isang orthonormal basis.\n"
"Isang prosedura na kilala bilang *Gram–Schmidt orthogonalization process* ang maaaring gamitin para buuin ang mga vector na ito.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Orthonormal sets and unitary matrices {#orthonormal-sets-and-unitary-matrices}"
msgstr "Mga orthonormal set at unitary matrix {#orthonormal-sets-and-unitary-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Orthonormal sets of vectors are closely connected with unitary matrices.\n"
"One way to express this connection is to say that the following three statements are logically equivalent (meaning that they are all true or all false) for any choice of a square matrix $U$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga orthonormal set ng vector ay may malapit na koneksyon sa mga unitary matrix.\n"
"Isang paraan ng pagpapahayag ng koneksyong ito ay ang pagsasabi na ang sumusunod na tatlong pahayag ay logically equivalent (ibig sabihin, lahat sila ay totoo o lahat sila ay mali) para sa anumang pagpipilian ng isang square matrix na $U$:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The matrix $U$ is unitary (that is, $U^{\\dagger} U = \\mathbb{I} = U U^{\\dagger}$).\n"
msgstr "Ang matrix na $U$ ay unitary (ibig sabihin, $U^{\\dagger} U = \\mathbb{I} = U U^{\\dagger}$).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The rows of $U$ form an orthonormal set.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga row ng $U$ ay bumubuo ng isang orthonormal set.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The columns of $U$ form an orthonormal set.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga column ng $U$ ay bumubuo ng isang orthonormal set.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This equivalence is actually pretty straightforward when we think about how matrix multiplication and the conjugate transpose work.\n"
"Suppose, for instance, that we have a $3\\times 3$ matrix like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang equivalence na ito ay medyo diretso kapag iniisip natin kung paano gumagana ang matrix multiplication at ang conjugate transpose.\n"
"Ipagpalagay, halimbawa, na mayroon tayong $3\\times 3$ na matrix tulad nito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The conjugate transpose of $U$ looks like this:\n"
msgstr "Ang conjugate transpose ng $U$ ay ganito ang hitsura:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiplying the two matrices, with the conjugate transpose on the left-hand side, gives us this matrix:\n"
msgstr "Ang pagpaparami ng dalawang matrix, na may conjugate transpose sa kaliwang bahagi, ay nagbibigay sa atin ng matrix na ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\quad &=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\quad &=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we form three vectors from the columns of $U$,\n"
msgstr "Kung babuo tayo ng tatlong vector mula sa mga column ng $U$,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_2\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_3\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_2\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_3\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then we can alternatively express the product above as follows:\n"
msgstr "maaari nating ipahayag ang product sa itaas sa ganitong paraan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Referring to the equation $(3)$, we now see that the condition that this matrix is equal to the identity matrix is equivalent to the orthonormality of the set $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_3\\rangle\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Tumutukoy sa equation $(3)$, makikita na ngayon natin na ang kondisyon na ang matrix na ito ay katumbas ng identity matrix ay katumbas ng orthonormality ng set na $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_3\\rangle\\}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This argument generalizes to unitary matrices of any size.\n"
"The fact that the rows of a matrix form an orthonormal basis if and only if the matrix is unitary then follows from the fact that a matrix is unitary if and only if its transpose is unitary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang argumentong ito ay nag-generalize sa mga unitary matrix ng anumang laki.\n"
"Ang katotohanan na ang mga row ng isang matrix ay bumubuo ng isang orthonormal basis kung at tanging kung ang matrix ay unitary ay sumusunod mula sa katotohanang ang isang matrix ay unitary kung at tanging kung ang transpose nito ay unitary.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the equivalence described above, together with the fact that every orthonormal set can be extended to form an orthonormal basis, we conclude the following useful fact:\n"
"Given any orthonormal set of vectors $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ drawn from an $n$-dimensional space, there exists a unitary matrix $U$ whose first $m$ columns are the vectors $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$.\n"
"Pictorially, we can always find a unitary matrix having this form:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil sa equivalence na inilarawan sa itaas, kasama ang katotohanang ang bawat orthonormal set ay maaaring mapalawak para bumuo ng isang orthonormal basis, maaari nating tapusin ang sumusunod na kapaki-pakinabang na katotohanan:\n"
"Dahil ang anumang orthonormal set ng mga vector na $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ na kinuha mula sa isang $n$-dimensional na espasyo, may isang unitary matrix na $U$ na ang unang $m$ column nito ay ang mga vector na $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$.\n"
"Pictorially, palagi tayong makakahanap ng unitary matrix na may ganitong anyo:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\left(\n"
"  \\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\\\\\n"
"    \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle & \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_m\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle &\n"
"    \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\n"
"  \\end{array}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\left(\n"
"  \\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\\\\\n"
"    \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle & \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_m\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle &\n"
"    \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\n"
"  \\end{array}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, the last $n-m$ columns are filled in with any choice of vectors $\\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ that make\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ an orthonormal basis.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito, ang huling $n-m$ na column ay pinupunan ng anumang pagpipilian ng mga vector na $\\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ na nagpapagawa ng\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ na isang orthonormal basis.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projections and projective measurements {#projections-and-projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Mga projection at projective measurement {#projections-and-projective-measurements}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projection matrices {#projection-matrices}"
msgstr "Mga projection matrix {#projection-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A square matrix $\\Pi$ is called a *projection* if it satisfies two properties:\n"
msgstr "Ang isang square matrix na $\\Pi$ ay tinatawag na *projection* kung nasasatisfy nito ang dalawang property:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '  1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Pi = \\Pi^{\\dagger}$.\n"
msgstr "$\\Pi = \\Pi^{\\dagger}$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '  2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Pi^2 = \\Pi$.\n"
msgstr "$\\Pi^2 = \\Pi$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrices that satisfy the first condition — that they are equal to their own conjugate transpose — are called *Hermitian matrices*, and matrices that satisfy the second condition — that squaring them leaves them unchanged — are called *idempotent* matrices.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga matrix na tumutugon sa unang kondisyon — na katumbas sila ng sarili nilang conjugate transpose — ay tinatawag na *Hermitian matrix*, at ang mga matrix na tumutugon sa ikalawang kondisyon — na ang pag-square sa kanila ay nag-iiwan sa kanila na walang pagbabago — ay tinatawag na *idempotent* na mga matrix.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a word of caution, the word *projection* is sometimes used to refer to any matrix that satisfies just the second condition but not necessarily the first, and when this is done the term *orthogonal projection* is typically used to refer to matrices satisfying both properties.\n"
"In the context of quantum information and computation, however, the terms *projection* and *projection matrix* more typically refer to matrices satisfying both conditions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilang babala, ang salitang *projection* ay minsan ginagamit para tumukoy sa anumang matrix na tumutugon lamang sa ikalawang kondisyon ngunit hindi kinakailangan ang una, at kapag ganito, ang terminong *orthogonal projection* ay karaniwang ginagamit para tumukoy sa mga matrix na tumutugon sa parehong kondisyon.\n"
"Sa konteksto ng quantum information at computation, gayunman, ang mga terminong *projection* at *projection matrix* ay mas karaniwang tumutukoy sa mga matrix na tumutugon sa parehong kondisyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An example of a projection is the matrix\n"
msgstr "Isang halimbawa ng projection ay ang matrix\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for any unit vector $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$.\n"
"We can see that this matrix is Hermitian as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa anumang unit vector na $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$.\n"
"Maaari nating makita na ang matrix na ito ay Hermitian tulad nito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger} = \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\bigl( \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger} = \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\bigl( \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, to obtain the second equality, we have used the formula\n"
msgstr "Dito, para makuha ang ikalawang pagkakapantay-pantay, ginamit natin ang formula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(A B)^{\\dagger} = B^{\\dagger} A^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(A B)^{\\dagger} = B^{\\dagger} A^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is always true, for any two matrices $A$ and $B$ for which the product $AB$ makes sense.\n"
msgstr "na laging totoo, para sa anumang dalawang matrix na $A$ at $B$ kung saan makatuwiran ang product na $AB$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To see that the matrix $\\Pi$ in $(4)$ is idempotent, we can use the assumption that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is a unit vector, so that it satisfies $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi\\rangle = 1$.\n"
"Thus, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Para makita na ang matrix na $\\Pi$ sa $(4)$ ay idempotent, maaari nating gamitin ang asumpsyon na ang $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ay isang unit vector, kaya't nasasatisfy nito ang $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi\\rangle = 1$.\n"
"Kaya, mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"= \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert \\bigr)^2\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"= \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert \\bigr)^2\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More generally, if $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is any orthonormal set of vectors, then the matrix\n"
msgstr "Sa mas pangkalahatang paraan, kung ang $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ ay anumang orthonormal set ng mga vector, ang matrix na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{5}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{5}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is a projection.\n"
"Specifically, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"ay isang projection.\n"
"Partikular, mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger}\n"
"&= \\biggl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\bigl(\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert\\bigr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"&= \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger}\n"
"&= \\biggl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\bigl(\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert\\bigr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"&= \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and\n"
msgstr "at\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"& = \\biggl( \\sum_{j = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{j = 1}^m\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert  \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"& = \\biggl( \\sum_{j = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{j = 1}^m\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert  \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the orthonormality of $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ implies the second-to-last equality.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang orthonormality ng $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ ay nagpapahiwatig ng pangalawa hanggang huling pagkakapantay-pantay.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In fact, this exhausts all of the possibilities: *every* projection $\\Pi$ can be written in the form $(5)$ for some choice of an orthonormal set $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"(Technically speaking, the zero matrix $\\Pi=0$, which is a projection, is a special case.\n"
"To fit it into the general form $(5)$ we must allow the possibility that the sum is empty, resulting in the zero matrix.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa katunayan, ito ay sumasaklaw sa lahat ng posibilidad: ang *bawat* projection na $\\Pi$ ay maaaring isulat sa anyo $(5)$ para sa ilang pagpipilian ng isang orthonormal set na $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"(Teknikalisyong nagsasalita, ang zero matrix na $\\Pi=0$, na isang projection, ay isang espesyal na kaso.\n"
"Para mailagay ito sa pangkalahatang anyo $(5)$ kailangan nating payagan ang posibilidad na ang sum ay walang laman, na nagbibigay ng zero matrix.)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projective measurements {#projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Mga projective measurement {#projective-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The notion of a measurement of a quantum system is more general than just standard basis measurements.\n"
"*Projective measurements* are measurements that are described by a collection of projections whose sum is equal to the identity matrix.\n"
"In symbols, a collection $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ of projection matrices describes a projective measurement if\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang konsepto ng pagsukat ng isang quantum system ay mas pangkalahatan kaysa sa simpleng standard basis measurement.\n"
"Ang mga *projective measurement* ay mga pagsukat na inilarawan ng isang koleksyon ng mga projection na ang sum ay katumbas ng identity matrix.\n"
"Sa simbolo, ang isang koleksyon na $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ ng mga projection matrix ay naglalarawan ng isang projective measurement kung\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When such a measurement is performed on a system $\\mathsf{X}$ while it is in some state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, two things happen:\n"
msgstr "Kapag ang ganitong pagsukat ay isinagawa sa isang sistema na $\\mathsf{X}$ habang ito ay nasa ilang estado na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, dalawang bagay ang nangyayari:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, the outcome of the measurement is $k$ with probability equal to\n"
msgstr "Para sa bawat $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, ang resulta ng pagsukat ay $k$ na may probabilidad na katumbas ng\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $k$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $k$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For whichever outcome $k$ the measurement produces, the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes\n"
msgstr "Para sa anumang resulta na $k$ na nailabas ng pagsukat, ang estado ng $\\mathsf{X}$ ay nagiging\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also choose outcomes other than $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ for projective measurements if we wish.\n"
"More generally, for any finite and nonempty set $\\Sigma$, if we have a collection of projection matrices\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari rin tayong pumili ng mga resulta na iba sa $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ para sa mga projective measurement kung nais natin.\n"
"Sa mas pangkalahatang paraan, para sa anumang finite at hindi walang laman na set na $\\Sigma$, kung mayroon tayong koleksyon ng mga projection matrix\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_a:a\\in\\Sigma\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_a:a\\in\\Sigma\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "that satisfies the condition\n"
msgstr "na tumutugon sa kondisyon\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\Pi_a = \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\Pi_a = \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then this collection describes a projective measurement whose possible outcomes coincide with the set $\\Sigma$, where the rules are the same as before:\n"
msgstr "kung gayon ang koleksyong ito ay naglalarawan ng isang projective measurement na ang mga posibleng resulta ay tumutugma sa set na $\\Sigma$, kung saan ang mga panuntunan ay kapareho ng dati:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each $a\\in\\Sigma$, the outcome of the measurement is $a$ with probability equal to\n"
msgstr "Para sa bawat $a\\in\\Sigma$, ang resulta ng pagsukat ay $a$ na may probabilidad na katumbas ng\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $a$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $a$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For whichever outcome $a$ the measurement produces, the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes\n"
msgstr "Para sa anumang resulta na $a$ na nailabas ng pagsukat, ang estado ng $\\mathsf{X}$ ay nagiging\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, standard basis measurements are equivalent to projective measurements, where $\\Sigma$ is the set of classical states of whatever system $\\mathsf{X}$ we're talking about and our set of projection matrices is\n"
"$\\{\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert:a\\in\\Sigma\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa, ang mga standard basis measurement ay katumbas ng mga projective measurement, kung saan ang $\\Sigma$ ay ang set ng mga classical state ng anumang sistema na $\\mathsf{X}$ na pinag-uusapan natin at ang ating set ng mga projection matrix ay\n"
"$\\{\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert:a\\in\\Sigma\\}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Another example of a projective measurement, this time on two qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$, is given by the set\n"
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\Pi_1\\}$, where\n"
msgstr ""
"Isa pang halimbawa ng projective measurement, sa pagkakataong ito sa dalawang qubit na $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$, ay ibinibigay ng set\n"
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\Pi_1\\}$, kung saan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\langle \\phi^+ \\vert + \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\langle \\phi^- \\vert + \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\langle \\psi^+ \\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\langle \\phi^+ \\vert + \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\langle \\phi^- \\vert + \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\langle \\psi^+ \\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we have multiple systems that are jointly in some quantum state and a projective measurement is performed on just one of the systems, the action is similar to what we had for standard basis measurements — and in fact we can now describe this action in much simpler terms than we could before.\n"
msgstr "Kung mayroon tayong maraming sistema na magkasamang nasa ilang quantum state at isang projective measurement ang isinasagawa sa isa lamang sa mga sistema, ang aksyon ay katulad ng mayroon tayo para sa mga standard basis measurement — at sa katunayan maaari na nating ilarawan ang aksyong ito sa mas simpleng termino kaysa kaya natin noon.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be precise, let us suppose that we have two systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ in a quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, and a projective measurement described by a collection $\\{\\Pi_a : a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ is performed on the system $\\mathsf{X}$, while nothing is done to $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Doing this is then equivalent to performing the projective measurement described by the collection\n"
msgstr ""
"Para maging tumpak, ipagpalagay na mayroon tayong dalawang sistema na $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ sa isang quantum state na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, at isang projective measurement na inilarawan ng koleksyon na $\\{\\Pi_a : a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ ay isinasagawa sa sistema na $\\mathsf{X}$, habang walang ginagawa sa $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Ang paggawa nito ay katumbas ng pagsukat na projective na inilarawan ng koleksyon\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"on the joint system $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
"Each measurement outcome $a$ results with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"sa joint system na $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
"Ang bawat resulta ng pagsukat na $a$ ay nangyayari na may probabilidad\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and conditioned on the result $a$ appearing, the state of the joint system $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ becomes\n"
msgstr "at nakondisyon sa paglabas ng resulta na $a,$ ang estado ng joint system na $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ ay nagiging\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{(\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{(\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementing projective measurements {#implementing-projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Pagpapatupad ng mga projective measurement {#implementing-projective-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Arbitrary projective measurements can be implemented using unitary operations, standard basis measurements, and an extra workspace system, as will now be explained.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga arbitrary na projective measurement ay maaaring ipatupad gamit ang mga unitary operation, standard basis measurement, at isang karagdagang workspace system, gaya ng ipapaliwanag ngayon.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ is a system and $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ is a projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$. We can easily generalize this discussion to projective measurements having different sets of outcomes, but in the interest of convenience and simplicity we will assume the set of possible outcomes for our measurement is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Ipagpalagay na ang $\\mathsf{X}$ ay isang sistema at ang $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ ay isang projective measurement sa $\\mathsf{X}$. Madali nating ma-generalize ang talakayan na ito sa mga projective measurement na may iba't ibang set ng mga resulta, ngunit para sa kaginhawahan at pagiging simple ay ipapalagay natin na ang set ng mga posibleng resulta para sa ating pagsukat ay $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us note explicitly that $m$ is not necessarily equal to the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ — we'll let $n$ be the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$, which means that each matrix $\\Pi_k$ is an $n\\times n$ projection matrix.\n"
msgstr "Pansinin natin nang malinaw na ang $m$ ay hindi kinakailangang katumbas ng bilang ng mga classical state ng $\\mathsf{X}$ — hahayaan nating ang $n$ ang bilang ng mga classical state ng $\\mathsf{X}$, na nangangahulugang ang bawat matrix na $\\Pi_k$ ay isang $n\\times n$ na projection matrix.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because we assume that $\\{\\Pi_0\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ represents a projective measurement, it is necessarily the case that\n"
msgstr "Dahil ipinapalagay natin na ang $\\{\\Pi_0\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ ay kumakatawan sa isang projective measurement, kinakailangan na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\Pi_k = \\mathbb{I}_n.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\Pi_k = \\mathbb{I}_n.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our goal is to perform a process that has the same effect as performing this projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$, but to do this using only unitary operations and standard basis measurements.\n"
msgstr "Ang ating layunin ay magsagawa ng proseso na may parehong epekto sa pagganap ng projective measurement na ito sa $\\mathsf{X}$, ngunit gawin ito gamit lamang ang mga unitary operation at standard basis measurement.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will make use of an extra workspace system $\\mathsf{Y}$ to do this, and specifically we'll take the classical state set of $\\mathsf{Y}$ to be $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, which is the same as the set of outcomes of the projective measurement.\n"
"The idea is that we will perform a standard basis measurement on $\\mathsf{Y}$, and interpret the outcome of this measurement as being equivalent to the outcome of the projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"We'll need to assume that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is initialized to some fixed state, which we'll choose to be $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"(Any other choice of fixed quantum state vector could be made to work, but choosing $\\vert 0\\rangle$ makes the explanation to follow much simpler.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Gagamitin natin ang karagdagang workspace system na $\\mathsf{Y}$ para gawin ito, at partikular na kukuha tayo ng classical state set ng $\\mathsf{Y}$ na $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, na kapareho ng set ng mga resulta ng projective measurement.\n"
"Ang ideya ay magsasagawa tayo ng standard basis measurement sa $\\mathsf{Y}$, at bibigyang-kahulugan ang resulta ng pagsukat na ito bilang katumbas ng resulta ng projective measurement sa $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Kakailanganin nating ipagpalagay na ang $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay na-initialize sa ilang fixed state, na pipiliin nating $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"(Ang anumang ibang pagpipilian ng fixed quantum state vector ay maaaring gawing gumana, ngunit ang pagpili ng $\\vert 0\\rangle$ ay nagpapadali ng paliwanag na susunod.)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, in order for a standard basis measurement of $\\mathsf{Y}$ to tell us anything about $\\mathsf{X}$, we will need to allow $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ to interact somehow before measuring $\\mathsf{Y}$, by performing a unitary operation on the system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$.\n"
"First consider this matrix:\n"
msgstr ""
"Siyempre, para ang standard basis measurement ng $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay makapagbigay ng impormasyon tungkol sa $\\mathsf{X}$, kakailanganin nating payagan ang $\\mathsf{X}$ at $\\mathsf{Y}$ na makipag-ugnayan sa isa't isa bago sukatin ang $\\mathsf{Y}$, sa pamamagitan ng pagsasagawa ng unitary operation sa sistema na $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$.\n"
"Una, isaalang-alang ang matrix na ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\Pi_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\Pi_k.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expressed explicitly as a so-called *block matrix*, which is essentially a matrix of matrices that we interpret as a single, larger matrix, $M$ looks like this:\n"
msgstr "Ipinahayag nang malinaw bilang isang tinatawag na *block matrix*, na mahalagang isang matrix ng mga matrix na binibigyang-kahulugan natin bilang isang mas malaking matrix, ang $M$ ay ganito ang hitsura:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, each $0$ represents an $n\\times n$ matrix filled entirely with zeros, so that the entire matrix $M$ is an $nm\\times nm$ matrix.\n"
msgstr "Dito, ang bawat $0$ ay kumakatawan sa isang $n\\times n$ na matrix na puno ng mga zero, kaya ang buong matrix na $M$ ay isang $nm\\times nm$ na matrix.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, $M$ is certainly not a unitary matrix (unless $m=1$, in which case $\\Pi_0 = \\mathbb{I}$, giving $M = \\mathbb{I}$ in this trivial case) because unitary matrices cannot have any columns (or rows) that are entirely $0$; unitary matrices have columns that form orthonormal bases, and the all-zero vector is not a unit vector.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, ang $M$ ay tiyak na hindi isang unitary matrix (maliban kung ang $m=1,$ kung saan ang $\\Pi_0 = \\mathbb{I},$ na nagbibigay ng $M = \\mathbb{I}$ sa trivial na kasong ito) dahil ang mga unitary matrix ay hindi maaaring magkaroon ng anumang mga column (o row) na puro $0;$ ang mga unitary matrix ay may mga column na bumubuo ng mga orthonormal basis, at ang all-zero vector ay hindi isang unit vector.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, it is the case that the first $n$ columns of $M$ are orthonormal, and we get this from the assumption that $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ is a measurement.\n"
"To verify this claim, notice that for each $j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, the vector formed by column number $j$ of $M$ is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Gayunpaman, totoo na ang unang $n$ na column ng matrix na $M$ ay orthonormal, at nakuha natin ito mula sa asumpsyon na ang $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ ay isang pagsukat.\n"
"Para i-verify ang claim na ito, pansinin na para sa bawat $j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, ang vector na nabuo ng column number $j$ ng $M$ ay ang sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle = M \\vert 0, j\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle = M \\vert 0, j\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that here we're numbering the columns starting from column $0$. Taking the inner product of column $i$ with column $j$ when $i,j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ gives\n"
msgstr "Pansinin na dito ang bilang ng mga column ay nagsisimula sa column $0$. Ang pagkuha ng inner product ng column $i$ sa column $j$ kapag ang $i,j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ ay nagbibigay ng\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_i \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert i\\rangle\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1} \\vert l \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle k \\vert l \\rangle \\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle i \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\vert j \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & i = j\\\\\n"
"0 & i\\neq j,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_i \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert i\\rangle\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1} \\vert l \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle k \\vert l \\rangle \\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle i \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\vert j \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & i = j\\\\\n"
"0 & i\\neq j,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is what we needed to show.\n"
msgstr "na siyang kailangan nating ipakita.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, because the first $n$ columns of the matrix $M$ are orthonormal, we can replace all of the remaining zero entries by some different choice of complex number entries so that the entire matrix is unitary.\n"
msgstr "Kaya, dahil ang unang $n$ na column ng matrix na $M$ ay orthonormal, maaari nating palitan ang lahat ng natitirang zero entry ng ibang pagpipilian ng mga complex number entry upang ang buong matrix ay maging unitary.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we're given the matrices $\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}$, we can compute suitable matrices to fill in for the blocks marked $\\fbox{?}$ in the equation — using the Gram–Schmidt process — but it does not matter specifically what these matrices are for the sake of this discussion.\n"
msgstr "Kung ibinibigay sa atin ang mga matrix na $\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}$, maaari tayong mag-compute ng angkop na mga matrix para punan ang mga block na minarkahan ng $\\fbox{?}$ sa equation — gamit ang Gram–Schmidt process — ngunit hindi mahalaga kung ano specifically ang mga matrix na ito para sa layunin ng talakayan na ito.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally we can describe the measurement process: we first perform $U$ on the joint system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ and then measure $\\mathsf{Y}$ with respect to a standard basis measurement.\n"
"For an arbitrary state $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ of $\\mathsf{X}$, we obtain the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas maaari na nating ilarawan ang proseso ng pagsukat: una ay isasagawa natin ang $U$ sa joint system na $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ at pagkatapos ay susukatin ang $\\mathsf{Y}$ gamit ang standard basis measurement.\n"
"Para sa isang arbitrary na estado na $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ ng $\\mathsf{X}$, makukuha natin ang estado\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= M \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= M \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the first equality follows from the fact that $U$ and $M$ agree on their first $n$ columns.\n"
"When we perform a projective measurement on $\\mathsf{Y}$, we obtain each outcome $k$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang unang pagkakapantay-pantay ay sumusunod mula sa katotohanang nagkakasundo ang $U$ at $M$ sa kanilang unang $n$ na column.\n"
"Kapag nagsagawa tayo ng projective measurement sa $\\mathsf{Y}$, makukuha natin ang bawat resulta na $k$ na may probabilidad\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "in which case the state of $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ becomes\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang estado ng $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ ay nagiging\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, $\\mathsf{Y}$ stores a copy of the measurement outcome and $\\mathsf{X}$ changes precisely as it would had the projective measurement described by $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ been performed directly on $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr "Kaya, ang $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay nag-iimbak ng kopya ng resulta ng pagsukat at ang $\\mathsf{X}$ ay nagbabago nang eksakto gaya ng magiging kaso kung ang projective measurement na inilarawan ng $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ ay direktang isinagawa sa $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
